WEBVTT

1
00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:47.333
[airplane, radio transmissions]

2
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.850
(Captain Over Radio)...request
permission to enter US airspace.

3
00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:05.180
(Virginia Vallejo) I've had to
leave a house in the middle of

4
00:01:05.274 --> 00:01:07.436
the night because
of a man before...

5
00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:11.186
but this is the first time
I've had to leave a country.

6
00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.614
(Tower Over Radio) 7221,
you are cleared to enter.

7
00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.738
(Captain) Okay, folks,
we are now entering

8
00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:19.114
United States airspace.

9
00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:20.740
(Shepard) You're safe now.

10
00:01:37.598 --> 00:01:39.430
(Virginia)
I've made this trip before.

11
00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:43.552
There were always dozens
of white roses waiting

12
00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:47.059
for me in every suite but
the men waiting at the door

13
00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:49.516
did not wear uniforms.

14
00:01:50.694 --> 00:01:52.401
They wore Armani.

15
00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:05.540
So, Virginia over the next few
days you'll nneet with officials

16
00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:08.869
from the Justice Department and
they will inform you of the

17
00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.124
procedure to follow from now on.

18
00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.752
Can someone get me
an aspirin please?

19
00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:16.759
My head is going to explode.

20
00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:19.633
(Holland) Ma'am, for your own
safety, you do not leave this

21
00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:21.510
room or communicate with anyone.

22
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.933
I have two of my men
standing outside.

23
00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.477
Do you understand?

24
00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:34.360
Can you get them to bring
me an aspirin please?

25
00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:38.448
Virginia, American hotels don't
give out aspirin anymore.

26
00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:40.741
It's considered a
drug in this country.

27
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:49.000
[laughs]

28
00:03:00.514 --> 00:03:03.427
(Virginia VO) Pablo would
have laughed at that, too.

29
00:03:04.685 --> 00:03:07.678
Then he would have
had them all killed.

30
00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:10.434
♪♪

31
00:03:55.527 --> 00:03:56.358
[crash, neighing horse]

32
00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:34.059
(Careta) We have to
finish him, Patrón.

33
00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:36.474
[cocking guns]

34
00:04:37.861 --> 00:04:39.443
(Escobar) Do it, Pelao.

35
00:04:42.365 --> 00:04:43.776
[neighing]

36
00:04:45.035 --> 00:04:46.321
[gun shot]

37
00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:06.174
(Escobar)
Did you see the guest list?

38
00:05:06.807 --> 00:05:09.299
(Victoria) Hmm. It's
full of beautiful women.

39
00:05:09.392 --> 00:05:12.430
Colombia is full of
beautiful women, my love.

40
00:05:12.521 --> 00:05:14.137
It's a party.

41
00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:15.767
Actresses, beauty queens.

42
00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:18.065
And soccer players,
union delegates.

43
00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.147
You are much more beautiful.
Look.

44
00:05:21.238 --> 00:05:22.649
Than the union delegates?

45
00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:24.196
Look who's coming.

46
00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.241
I don't like it, Pablo.

47
00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.660
Business and family separate.

48
00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:31.487
We already talked about it.

49
00:05:31.581 --> 00:05:32.947
I know, I know.
With the party,

50
00:05:33.041 --> 00:05:35.624
everything is a little bit of
a mess. I'll take care of it.

51
00:05:41.925 --> 00:05:43.336
[door closes]

52
00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:46.423
(Salvador) I have the
triggerman you asked for.

53
00:05:46.513 --> 00:05:47.970
I'll talk to him, and
you take him away.

54
00:05:48.056 --> 00:05:48.921
I don't want him around.

55
00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.098
Don Pablo.
Don Pablo.

56
00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.018
If you can find this coin,
you can keep it. Go for it.

57
00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:05.858
I have a little
job for you in Leticia.

58
00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:08.612
There's a file from seven years
ago linking me to the murder

59
00:06:08.702 --> 00:06:11.445
of two DAS agents. You have
to make it disappear, okay?

60
00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:12.574
Everything you find.

61
00:06:12.914 --> 00:06:14.405
Leave it nice and clean.

62
00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:17.116
Listen, you have
contacts there, right?

63
00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.627
My cousin's wife works
at the courthouse.

64
00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:22.046
She can get me in.
There's no problem.

65
00:06:22.132 --> 00:06:22.918
...Dad?

66
00:06:23.508 --> 00:06:25.750
...I don't care if you have to
take out somebody, or what you

67
00:06:25.844 --> 00:06:28.678
have to do. You can burn the
building down if you want...

68
00:06:29.556 --> 00:06:31.343
but get rid of that file.

69
00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:36.390
You have 30,000 for expenses,
for travelling, for ammunition,

70
00:06:36.479 --> 00:06:37.811
for rumba, for everything.

71
00:06:37.898 --> 00:06:40.732
If you run out, ask
Salvador for more. He will...

72
00:06:40.817 --> 00:06:42.558
...Dad!
...take care of everything.

73
00:06:42.903 --> 00:06:45.145
...Go on then. Go on.
...You got it, boss.

74
00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.103
You find the coin?

75
00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:47.278
It's only five pesos.

76
00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:49.448
It's only five pesos? Don
Pablo, you know how hard

77
00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:51.821
your daddy has to work
to make some money?

78
00:06:51.912 --> 00:06:52.868
Give it back.

79
00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.871
Only five pesos.

80
00:06:55.957 --> 00:06:59.121
♪♪

81
00:07:00.211 --> 00:07:02.328
Is that the hacienda down there?

82
00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:05.381
(Victor) We've been flying
over it for a while, my love.

83
00:07:28.239 --> 00:07:29.525
We're getting kidnapped!

84
00:07:29.616 --> 00:07:32.029
It's okay, Virgie. Calm down.

85
00:07:33.078 --> 00:07:34.194
It's not okay.

86
00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:36.244
Do you know how much all
of us here are worth?

87
00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:40.867
(VO) We'd all heard
about or host,

88
00:07:40.961 --> 00:07:42.918
but none of us had ever met him.

89
00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:46.668
His name is at the top of the
list of the nouveau riche.

90
00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:50.627
A group of young men that
have made huge fortunes

91
00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.757
in very little time.

92
00:07:57.978 --> 00:07:59.139
Welcome.

93
00:08:00.522 --> 00:08:03.060
Please don't mind the weapons,
they're there for the animals.

94
00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:05.311
We have a little zoo here.
You like to see it?

95
00:08:05.402 --> 00:08:07.485
You scared us to death.

96
00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.779
Tell our host, this is
no way to welcome guests.

97
00:08:10.865 --> 00:08:12.447
As soon as I see him.

98
00:08:24.087 --> 00:08:26.124
[elephant trumpets]

99
00:08:29.676 --> 00:08:30.883
(Chantal) Oh, my God.

100
00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:33.006
They're beautiful.

101
00:08:33.096 --> 00:08:34.837
They're very happy here.

102
00:08:34.931 --> 00:08:36.047
They like Colombia.

103
00:08:37.142 --> 00:08:39.555
That's because they
don't read the papers.

104
00:08:44.774 --> 00:08:46.515
This house is gigantic.

105
00:08:47.444 --> 00:08:49.652
I don't see the
servants anywhere.

106
00:08:50.447 --> 00:08:51.813
There you have them.

107
00:08:52.866 --> 00:08:57.110
(VO) This new elite has
its own social structure.

108
00:08:58.079 --> 00:09:02.824
Down in the corridors, the
soldiers, young, uneducated men

109
00:09:02.917 --> 00:09:05.910
from the slums, warriors
in the organization.

110
00:09:07.505 --> 00:09:10.464
They're nothing like the humble
servants working on the ranches

111
00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.418
of the traditionally rich
people in my country.

112
00:09:13.511 --> 00:09:15.218
They are confident.

113
00:09:15.305 --> 00:09:18.423
They handle security
and operations, and...

114
00:09:22.604 --> 00:09:24.596
...have good taste in women.

115
00:09:27.776 --> 00:09:30.519
(Woman) Virginia,
I never miss your show!

116
00:09:30.612 --> 00:09:32.274
You look so beautiful.

117
00:09:38.953 --> 00:09:40.865
(VO) Above them, the cream.

118
00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:46.250
Artists, businessmen, soccer
players, journalists, models.

119
00:09:47.545 --> 00:09:50.834
Always a perfect distance
away from our host.

120
00:09:52.008 --> 00:09:53.670
Cover your ears, Victor.

121
00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.878
There are so many
handsome guys here.

122
00:10:01.184 --> 00:10:02.095
Thank you.

123
00:10:02.185 --> 00:10:04.518
Anyone who's anyone is here.

124
00:10:06.689 --> 00:10:08.476
Where does he
make all this money?

125
00:10:09.025 --> 00:10:11.608
That's the question a
reporter has to ask.

126
00:10:18.034 --> 00:10:19.866
[applause]

127
00:10:20.245 --> 00:10:22.487
Good one, good one, good one!

128
00:10:31.131 --> 00:10:32.338
[applause]

129
00:10:37.971 --> 00:10:40.213
Virginia. Virginia.

130
00:10:42.142 --> 00:10:43.474
Where have you been hiding?

131
00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.392
Pablo keep asking for you.

132
00:10:45.478 --> 00:10:47.720
He's driving us
crazy, so come on.

133
00:10:48.815 --> 00:10:51.683
Victor, wait here.
Don't fall in love with a local.

134
00:10:57.866 --> 00:11:01.155
(VO) And up the hill, the
kings of the white mountain.

135
00:11:02.245 --> 00:11:05.204
We still don't know
their names but soon,

136
00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:07.873
there won't be a single
Colombian who doesn't.

137
00:11:08.877 --> 00:11:10.038
She was easy to find.

138
00:11:10.128 --> 00:11:12.165
I just went where all
the men were looking.

139
00:11:12.672 --> 00:11:13.788
Pablo?

140
00:11:13.882 --> 00:11:15.544
Pablo Escobar?

141
00:11:18.178 --> 00:11:19.385
No.

142
00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.553
Your complaints were passed on
to me, so I beg your pardon.

143
00:11:21.639 --> 00:11:22.800
You lied to me.

144
00:11:22.891 --> 00:11:24.473
Good Lord,
of course I lied to you.

145
00:11:24.559 --> 00:11:25.925
I didn't want you to leave.

146
00:11:28.021 --> 00:11:29.683
You look even
prettier in person.

147
00:11:29.772 --> 00:11:32.389
Then I'll have to
fire my makeup girl.

148
00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.227
There's a lot of talk
about you over there.

149
00:11:36.321 --> 00:11:38.438
Speculations about your past.

150
00:11:38.531 --> 00:11:41.194
No, no, no, don't
listen to that.

151
00:11:41.284 --> 00:11:43.822
I only listen when they
speculate about my future.

152
00:11:43.912 --> 00:11:45.153
I already know my past.

153
00:11:45.788 --> 00:11:47.450
And what's the occasion?

154
00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.782
It's just the
founding of a society.

155
00:11:49.876 --> 00:11:51.617
What kind of society?

156
00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:54.749
Philanthropic. We are
building houses for the poor.

157
00:11:54.839 --> 00:11:56.250
Nobody over
there mentioned to you

158
00:11:57.884 --> 00:11:58.624
No.

159
00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:01.627
Well, were going to build
2,000 homes for the people

160
00:12:01.721 --> 00:12:03.053
at the garbage dump.

161
00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:05.051
I got a very good
price on a lot.

162
00:12:05.141 --> 00:12:07.007
And where does the
money come from?

163
00:12:07.101 --> 00:12:09.013
What, is this an interview?

164
00:12:09.103 --> 00:12:10.435
I'm a journalist.

165
00:12:10.521 --> 00:12:11.978
Then come and see it.

166
00:12:13.024 --> 00:12:14.731
Come and see it.
I'll show it to you.

167
00:12:14.817 --> 00:12:16.604
It's good for the
country to know.

168
00:12:16.694 --> 00:12:18.401
Good for the country
or good for you?

169
00:12:19.155 --> 00:12:21.363
Am I not a part of the country?

170
00:12:25.662 --> 00:12:28.405
(VO) We weren't aware at the
time but that night we were

171
00:12:28.498 --> 00:12:31.957
celebrating the founding
of the Medellin Cartel and the

172
00:12:32.043 --> 00:12:34.581
crowning of Pablo as its king.

173
00:12:35.672 --> 00:12:38.756
Things were about
to change forever...

174
00:12:38.841 --> 00:12:41.128
in Colombia and in my life.

175
00:12:45.098 --> 00:12:46.805
[kids shouting]

176
00:13:05.285 --> 00:13:08.198
Breathe through your mouth
and you get used to it fast.

177
00:13:08.746 --> 00:13:10.032
Watch where you step.

178
00:13:10.123 --> 00:13:11.739
People dump bodies
out here sometimes.

179
00:13:11.833 --> 00:13:13.119
You're kidding.

180
00:13:17.213 --> 00:13:18.374
(Boy) Don Pablo!

181
00:13:19.924 --> 00:13:21.210
Don Pablo!

182
00:13:27.056 --> 00:13:28.718
Is everybody here named Pablo?

183
00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:30.970
(Priest) Everybody.
They named them after him.

184
00:13:31.644 --> 00:13:34.637
Listen, we are now
finishing the first 600 but

185
00:13:34.731 --> 00:13:37.394
we want to build 2000, eh? 2000.

186
00:13:44.615 --> 00:13:47.232
Please tell our viewers the
motivation and goal behind

187
00:13:47.327 --> 00:13:48.989
this wonderful initiative,

188
00:13:52.206 --> 00:13:55.324
Well, It is painful for us to
see so many children starving

189
00:13:55.418 --> 00:13:57.956
completely unprotected
by the government.

190
00:13:58.046 --> 00:14:01.460
And building these
houses for them

191
00:14:01.549 --> 00:14:04.713
helps us to create a country
that we always dreamed about.

192
00:14:05.345 --> 00:14:08.213
I love Colombia, and now
that we have the chance to give

193
00:14:08.306 --> 00:14:11.344
back to this beautiful country
that gave us so much that is

194
00:14:11.434 --> 00:14:12.891
exactly what we're doing.

195
00:14:13.561 --> 00:14:16.850
(VO) That day, I decide that
I don't care how Pablo makes

196
00:14:16.939 --> 00:14:19.773
his money,
only how he uses it.

197
00:14:19.859 --> 00:14:25.150
♪♪

198
00:14:44.425 --> 00:14:45.632
Do you know that people?

199
00:14:45.718 --> 00:14:47.550
[laughs]

200
00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:50.424
I like the way you laugh.

201
00:14:50.515 --> 00:14:51.756
You laugh like on your show.

202
00:14:51.849 --> 00:14:54.262
You are so relaxed on TV.
How do you do that?

203
00:14:54.352 --> 00:14:55.934
Do you think I
could ever do that?

204
00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.602
There are tricks.

205
00:14:57.688 --> 00:14:59.179
Are you after my job?

206
00:14:59.273 --> 00:15:00.639
No, I'm not.

207
00:15:03.611 --> 00:15:04.852
Are you married?

208
00:15:07.657 --> 00:15:09.068
Not by choice.

209
00:15:09.158 --> 00:15:10.649
What does he do?

210
00:15:11.411 --> 00:15:13.118
He's a plastic surgeon.

211
00:15:13.204 --> 00:15:15.992
We are separated, but he doesn't
want to sign the divorce.

212
00:15:16.082 --> 00:15:18.574
He doesn't want you
to get married again?

213
00:15:18.668 --> 00:15:20.034
No, he doesn't want
to have to marry one of

214
00:15:20.128 --> 00:15:21.710
his teenage girlfriends.

215
00:15:21.796 --> 00:15:22.832
Aahh.

216
00:15:24.841 --> 00:15:27.254
Well, that can be fixed.

217
00:15:30.388 --> 00:15:31.720
You'll talk to him?

218
00:15:39.147 --> 00:15:42.766
Look I don't like hanging around
with married women. I don't.

219
00:15:42.859 --> 00:15:46.023
So, next time we are going out,
you're not going be his wife.

220
00:15:46.821 --> 00:15:47.902
No?

221
00:15:47.989 --> 00:15:49.355
No.

222
00:15:49.449 --> 00:15:51.236
Will I be his widow?

223
00:15:53.786 --> 00:15:55.152
What do you take me for?

224
00:16:03.671 --> 00:16:04.582
[bell rings]

225
00:16:04.672 --> 00:16:05.913
(A.D.) Everyone ready?

226
00:16:06.007 --> 00:16:08.044
(Paula)
Virginia! Your lawyer called!

227
00:16:08.134 --> 00:16:10.091
Your ex signed the papers!

228
00:16:10.178 --> 00:16:13.012
(A.D.) We are on in three, two...
...What?

229
00:16:22.482 --> 00:16:24.769
(VO) To celebrate
me being free again,

230
00:16:24.859 --> 00:16:28.273
Pablo takes me to an island
paradise only he knows about.

231
00:16:29.405 --> 00:16:31.863
If you're going
to cry over a man,

232
00:16:31.949 --> 00:16:34.692
better in a private
jet than on a bus.

233
00:16:44.837 --> 00:16:46.794
[thumping]

234
00:16:59.477 --> 00:17:00.388
[grunt]

235
00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:07.812
Where are you going?

236
00:17:07.902 --> 00:17:09.188
They're waiting.

237
00:17:11.447 --> 00:17:12.608
Who?

238
00:17:13.533 --> 00:17:15.820
♪♪

239
00:17:18.871 --> 00:17:20.112
Do I look okay?

240
00:17:20.206 --> 00:17:21.492
You look perfect.

241
00:17:22.708 --> 00:17:24.700
(Careta) How's it going, Patrón?

242
00:17:25.378 --> 00:17:26.368
Ma'am.

243
00:17:26.462 --> 00:17:28.203
Let's make a deal,
you tell me your secrets

244
00:17:28.297 --> 00:17:30.334
and I'll tell you mine, okay?

245
00:17:34.679 --> 00:17:36.796
(VO) Our trip is
an excuse to attend a

246
00:17:36.889 --> 00:17:38.676
congress of drug traffickers.

247
00:17:43.813 --> 00:17:46.146
(Monje) Virginia, how are you?
When did you arrive?

248
00:17:46.232 --> 00:17:47.473
Today.

249
00:17:47.567 --> 00:17:50.025
(VO) Pablo introduces me to
his associates in the cartel.

250
00:17:50.111 --> 00:17:53.149
He shows me off to
them like a trophy.

251
00:17:53.239 --> 00:17:55.982
And I know that they're
also there to evaluate me.

252
00:17:56.867 --> 00:17:59.701
Between them, they
form a new social class,

253
00:17:59.787 --> 00:18:01.574
the narco millionaires.

254
00:18:01.664 --> 00:18:04.281
And I'm the only journalist
with exclusive access

255
00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:06.037
to their first summit.

256
00:18:06.127 --> 00:18:08.744
Thank you.
I'm going to get a drink.

257
00:18:08.838 --> 00:18:11.956
Stay close, Virginia. These
men can't be trusted, okay?

258
00:18:13.217 --> 00:18:15.334
(VO) The most illegal thing
I'd ever done before that

259
00:18:15.428 --> 00:18:17.465
day was to double park.

260
00:18:17.555 --> 00:18:18.545
[laughs]

261
00:18:18.639 --> 00:18:22.679
But the truth is never in
my life had I felt safer.

262
00:18:24.937 --> 00:18:27.054
(Cartel Member) All of our
priorities is labeled with a

263
00:18:27.148 --> 00:18:28.389
color that doesn't change.

264
00:18:28.983 --> 00:18:31.566
(VO) That night, they split
the United States of America

265
00:18:31.652 --> 00:18:34.611
among them.
Florida for the Medellin Cartel,

266
00:18:34.697 --> 00:18:36.984
New York for the Cali Cartel.

267
00:18:37.658 --> 00:18:40.321
The independents add their
shipments to Pablo's.

268
00:18:40.953 --> 00:18:43.616
They know that nobody
would ever dare to steal

269
00:18:43.706 --> 00:18:45.447
even one gram from him.

270
00:18:49.462 --> 00:18:52.955
Seeing him in his natural
habitat, is addictive.

271
00:18:57.428 --> 00:19:01.092
Thanks to those men, it is
going to snow cocaine in the US.

272
00:19:10.191 --> 00:19:11.807
[truck horn]

273
00:19:13.486 --> 00:19:15.022
(Woman) Honey, did you see that?

274
00:19:17.448 --> 00:19:18.734
[squealing tires]

275
00:19:22.953 --> 00:19:24.569
[cars honking]

276
00:19:26.415 --> 00:19:29.499
(Driver)
Hey, guys, are you nuts?

277
00:19:30.002 --> 00:19:31.243
What the fuck are you doing?

278
00:19:43.516 --> 00:19:46.600
(Officer) Stuck in a
jam on highway 75 heading

279
00:19:46.686 --> 00:19:48.973
southbound out of Temple.

280
00:19:54.193 --> 00:19:57.311
[low rumble]

281
00:19:58.531 --> 00:20:00.397
Holy shit.

282
00:20:01.992 --> 00:20:04.985
♪♪

283
00:20:20.761 --> 00:20:22.844
(Car Driver) What are you doing?
Are you fucking nuts!

284
00:20:23.556 --> 00:20:25.138
I almost killed you!

285
00:20:25.224 --> 00:20:27.716
(VO) They called them the
saints, because they make the

286
00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:30.678
miracle of
multiplication up there.

287
00:20:31.355 --> 00:20:32.687
Do the math.

288
00:20:32.773 --> 00:20:36.016
One kilo is worth
$7,000 here in Colombia.

289
00:20:37.111 --> 00:20:40.275
In the United States, they cut
it, add lactose and it becomes

290
00:20:40.364 --> 00:20:44.699
three kilos which are
worth 150,000 there.

291
00:20:45.661 --> 00:20:47.323
Is that a miracle or not?

292
00:20:55.546 --> 00:20:57.333
(Man) Oh, my God!
(Woman) Jim, Stop!

293
00:20:57.423 --> 00:20:58.789
[car honking]

294
00:20:58.883 --> 00:20:59.999
(Man) Oh, shit!

295
00:21:00.092 --> 00:21:04.757
♪♪

296
00:21:32.124 --> 00:21:33.956
(TV announcer)
From the White House,

297
00:21:34.043 --> 00:21:36.660
President and
Mrs. Ronald Reagan.

298
00:21:36.754 --> 00:21:38.666
A message on drugs.

299
00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.627
(Ronald Reagan) Despite our
best efforts, illegal cocaine

300
00:21:41.717 --> 00:21:44.710
is coming into our country
at alarming levels.

301
00:21:44.804 --> 00:21:47.467
It's especially damaging to
the young people on whom

302
00:21:47.556 --> 00:21:52.051
our future depends. So tonight,
from our family to yours,

303
00:21:52.144 --> 00:21:56.354
from our home to yours
thank you for joining us.

304
00:21:58.192 --> 00:22:01.685
America has accomplished so
much in these last few years...

305
00:22:02.404 --> 00:22:03.690
(Govt Official)
Welcome, Agent Shepard.

306
00:22:03.781 --> 00:22:05.317
The President is glad
to have you on board.

307
00:22:05.407 --> 00:22:06.898
...Thank you.
...This is Mr. Velarde,

308
00:22:06.992 --> 00:22:08.199
representing the
Colombian government.

309
00:22:08.285 --> 00:22:09.742
Nice to meet you.

310
00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:12.913
The President's worried
about the latest report.

311
00:22:13.707 --> 00:22:15.915
Cocaine is no longer the
drug of the jet set,

312
00:22:16.001 --> 00:22:17.333
it's reaching the middle class.

313
00:22:17.419 --> 00:22:18.409
You know what that means.

314
00:22:18.504 --> 00:22:20.166
It's coming in without control.

315
00:22:20.256 --> 00:22:21.963
80 percent is coming
from Colombia.

316
00:22:22.049 --> 00:22:25.042
We're working to have an old
bilateral treaty reactivated.

317
00:22:25.135 --> 00:22:27.969
(Velarde) The Extradition
Treaty. We'll catch the narcos

318
00:22:28.055 --> 00:22:29.796
and turn them over so
you can try them here.

319
00:22:30.432 --> 00:22:32.515
They don't fear the
judges in Colombia,

320
00:22:32.601 --> 00:22:34.843
they either bribe
them or kill them.

321
00:22:34.937 --> 00:22:36.599
But they do fear your justice.

322
00:22:36.689 --> 00:22:37.930
Is there a legal basis for this?

323
00:22:38.023 --> 00:22:41.187
The coke is produced in my
country, but it's consumed here.

324
00:22:41.277 --> 00:22:43.985
The crime is completed
in the United States.

325
00:22:44.864 --> 00:22:46.355
I brought a draft.

326
00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:49.191
The President knows your record.

327
00:22:49.285 --> 00:22:51.868
He wants you to monitor
the whole process.

328
00:22:51.954 --> 00:22:53.490
The President will
be over shortly.

329
00:22:53.581 --> 00:22:56.449
We are hoping to implement
this in the next day or so.

330
00:22:56.542 --> 00:22:58.955
(Nancy Reagan) Drugs take away
the dream from every child's

331
00:22:59.044 --> 00:23:01.582
heart and replace
it with a nightmare.

332
00:23:02.339 --> 00:23:05.298
And it's time
we in America stand up

333
00:23:05.384 --> 00:23:07.046
and replace those dreams.

334
00:23:07.428 --> 00:23:09.169
(Escobar) What are we, children?

335
00:23:09.263 --> 00:23:10.970
Don't we have judges here?

336
00:23:11.056 --> 00:23:14.049
No mother sends her children to
the neighbors to be punished.

337
00:23:14.143 --> 00:23:15.099
No.

338
00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:18.353
(Monje) What do
the lawyers have to say?

339
00:23:18.439 --> 00:23:19.930
Is this constitutional?

340
00:23:20.024 --> 00:23:21.105
Can it be appealed?

341
00:23:21.191 --> 00:23:22.807
(Ignacio Castro)
Yeah, it can be appealed.

342
00:23:22.902 --> 00:23:24.393
We have to knock it down.

343
00:23:24.486 --> 00:23:26.728
That treaty puts us in
danger to everyone here.

344
00:23:26.822 --> 00:23:28.654
Every one of you,
every one of us.

345
00:23:31.201 --> 00:23:33.944
We have to fight it from the
institutions, from inside.

346
00:23:34.705 --> 00:23:35.821
(Hermosilla) From Congress?

347
00:23:35.915 --> 00:23:37.076
It's the only way.

348
00:23:37.166 --> 00:23:38.873
Throw money at them, both sides.

349
00:23:38.959 --> 00:23:41.667
Conservatives and Liberals,
they all like the good stuff.

350
00:23:44.173 --> 00:23:46.085
The spotlight like
this, bad for business.

351
00:23:46.175 --> 00:23:47.916
And whatever they
look for in your house,

352
00:23:48.010 --> 00:23:49.546
they'll find in everyone else's.

353
00:23:49.637 --> 00:23:51.799
(Carlos Corral)
Listen to us, please.

354
00:23:51.889 --> 00:23:53.346
They'll go after you.

355
00:23:53.432 --> 00:23:56.300
Politics is a bitch.

356
00:23:56.393 --> 00:23:58.055
No, hermano.
It's the other way around.

357
00:23:58.145 --> 00:23:59.852
If you reach Congress,
they respect you.

358
00:23:59.939 --> 00:24:01.555
Why? Because you're one of them.

359
00:24:03.275 --> 00:24:06.689
You know how much it costs
to run for state council

360
00:24:06.779 --> 00:24:08.896
in Colombia?
Ten million pesos.

361
00:24:08.989 --> 00:24:10.696
Ten million pesos.

362
00:24:10.783 --> 00:24:14.072
And for Senator I think
it is between 100 and

363
00:24:14.161 --> 00:24:16.027
120 million pesos.

364
00:24:16.121 --> 00:24:19.785
1,500 million pesos more
or less, for president of

365
00:24:19.875 --> 00:24:22.618
the republic. Tell me who
can spend that kind of money?

366
00:24:22.711 --> 00:24:25.454
The son of a farmer?
A worker? No, no.

367
00:24:27.132 --> 00:24:29.249
Politics comes
down to money here.

368
00:24:29.343 --> 00:24:31.255
Democracy comes
down to money here.

369
00:24:31.345 --> 00:24:34.133
So we have plenty of money.

370
00:24:35.474 --> 00:24:36.715
[chuckles]

371
00:24:36.809 --> 00:24:38.801
You, Garza, what's so funny?

372
00:24:39.645 --> 00:24:41.511
(Garza) You should listen
to yourself, Pablito.

373
00:24:41.605 --> 00:24:44.018
You're already talking
like a politician!

374
00:24:44.108 --> 00:24:45.440
[chuckles]

375
00:24:45.526 --> 00:24:48.439
♪♪

376
00:25:07.214 --> 00:25:09.456
Sir, we have an appointment
with the candidate.

377
00:25:12.136 --> 00:25:13.092
(Campaign Manager)
Are they armed?

378
00:25:13.178 --> 00:25:15.420
Why of course they are,
they're my bodyguards.

379
00:25:15.514 --> 00:25:17.847
I'm sorry, sir. If they're
armed, they can't come in.

380
00:25:20.436 --> 00:25:22.302
They're carrying our
donation to your campaign.

381
00:25:22.396 --> 00:25:24.683
If they can't come in,
the donation can't either.

382
00:25:24.773 --> 00:25:27.641
So go ask your candidate
if that's what he wants.

383
00:25:39.204 --> 00:25:41.116
(VO) The cartel
bets on both horses.

384
00:25:41.206 --> 00:25:43.914
Why put money
on only one candidate

385
00:25:44.001 --> 00:25:45.537
when you can put money on both?

386
00:25:45.627 --> 00:25:48.495
That way, no matter
who wins, they win.

387
00:25:51.550 --> 00:25:54.133
The narco's planes carry
candidates during the day

388
00:25:54.219 --> 00:25:57.087
and fly to the United
States at night.

389
00:26:00.768 --> 00:26:02.885
And what do they
get in exchange?

390
00:26:04.188 --> 00:26:06.851
You defend the competency of the
Supreme Court to question the

391
00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:09.398
constitutionality of the
Extradition Treaty,

392
00:26:09.485 --> 00:26:12.148
it will be good for
all of us, Mr. Candidate.

393
00:26:12.237 --> 00:26:16.402
These gentlemen want to donate
25 million pesos to our campaign

394
00:26:16.492 --> 00:26:18.404
here in Antioquia.

395
00:26:19.620 --> 00:26:22.784
(VO) People call the
contributions made by the drug

396
00:26:22.873 --> 00:26:24.785
lords hot money.
Why?

397
00:26:24.875 --> 00:26:25.991
...It's okay.

398
00:26:26.085 --> 00:26:27.951
You can leave it on the floor.

399
00:26:28.045 --> 00:26:30.332
We'll find someone
to pick it up later.

400
00:26:33.342 --> 00:26:35.049
(VO) Because it burns.

401
00:26:35.135 --> 00:26:37.923
♪♪

402
00:26:38.013 --> 00:26:40.005
How far are you
going to take this, Pablo?

403
00:26:40.599 --> 00:26:41.931
We're doing fine.

404
00:26:42.017 --> 00:26:43.508
Don't we have enough?

405
00:26:43.602 --> 00:26:45.810
Mi amor, in Congress
I can get things done,

406
00:26:45.896 --> 00:26:47.103
I can help people, I...

407
00:26:47.189 --> 00:26:48.521
Help your family first.

408
00:26:49.566 --> 00:26:51.023
You have money, Pablo.

409
00:26:51.110 --> 00:26:52.942
You have us.
What more do you want?

410
00:26:53.028 --> 00:26:54.940
I want respect.

411
00:26:56.824 --> 00:26:58.031
Respect?

412
00:26:58.117 --> 00:26:59.983
Mmhmm. I want respect.

413
00:27:02.955 --> 00:27:05.242
I want my son to be proud of me.

414
00:27:06.125 --> 00:27:07.366
Is that so hard to understand?

415
00:27:07.459 --> 00:27:10.497
First, he'd have to see you,
Pablo, but you're never home.

416
00:27:11.463 --> 00:27:14.297
Don Pablo, mi amigo,
go to the living room.

417
00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:16.132
There's nothing on TV?

418
00:27:17.219 --> 00:27:19.586
Good Lord, who
bought him that car?

419
00:27:23.308 --> 00:27:26.301
Victoria, mi amor, don't you
want to be the First Lady?

420
00:27:27.813 --> 00:27:30.146
I'd settle for being
the only lady, Pablo.

421
00:27:30.232 --> 00:27:32.975
Oh, my God.
No, no, again.

422
00:27:33.068 --> 00:27:35.526
She's helping me with
my political campaign.

423
00:27:37.406 --> 00:27:39.773
I want respect, too, Pablo.
Like you.

424
00:27:39.867 --> 00:27:40.106
I respect...

425
00:27:41.410 --> 00:27:43.072
The difference is
yours is enough for me.

426
00:27:43.162 --> 00:27:43.993
I respect you.

427
00:27:44.079 --> 00:27:45.069
No, you don't.

428
00:27:45.164 --> 00:27:46.120
...I do.
...You don't.

429
00:27:46.206 --> 00:27:48.744
I'll prove it.
What do you want me to do? What?

430
00:27:48.834 --> 00:27:50.291
I'll do it. What?

431
00:27:51.628 --> 00:27:53.460
That bitch from TV.

432
00:27:54.423 --> 00:27:55.914
End it with her.

433
00:27:58.093 --> 00:28:01.177
I promise right
now it is over now.

434
00:28:03.015 --> 00:28:04.051
Now.

435
00:28:05.434 --> 00:28:06.470
Right now.

436
00:28:10.314 --> 00:28:12.601
I promise. I promise.

437
00:28:13.942 --> 00:28:15.228
I promise.

438
00:28:15.319 --> 00:28:16.480
It is over.

439
00:28:18.363 --> 00:28:19.604
Give me one
of those laughters.

440
00:28:19.698 --> 00:28:21.234
See, see?

441
00:28:24.786 --> 00:28:26.618
[laughter on TV]

442
00:28:36.924 --> 00:28:38.506
[grunting]

443
00:28:46.683 --> 00:28:49.801
We want a country like a
mother, generous and fertile,

444
00:28:49.895 --> 00:28:52.979
who shares her wealth
equally with her children,

445
00:28:53.065 --> 00:28:54.977
but who always looks
out for the weakest.

446
00:28:55.067 --> 00:28:56.683
[applause]

447
00:28:59.488 --> 00:29:03.357
We want a country like a mother
who defends her children from

448
00:29:03.450 --> 00:29:06.443
foreign aggression
without hesitation.

449
00:29:06.995 --> 00:29:08.531
Severe but understanding.

450
00:29:09.248 --> 00:29:12.412
Long live the mothers of
Colombia and our motherland.

451
00:29:13.168 --> 00:29:16.627
They will cry tears of blood the
day the first son is extradited.

452
00:29:19.591 --> 00:29:20.502
[cheering]

453
00:29:20.592 --> 00:29:22.208
(Tv Anchor)
Let's stay in Antioquia

454
00:29:22.302 --> 00:29:23.918
to see how election
day has gone.

455
00:29:24.012 --> 00:29:27.471
At this time, most of the
votes have been counted.

456
00:29:28.308 --> 00:29:31.597
For Alternativa Popular,
Movimiento de Renovación Liberal

457
00:29:31.687 --> 00:29:35.397
Pablo Escobar Gaviria has been
elected representative of the

458
00:29:35.482 --> 00:29:39.101
house of Medellin.
For Colombia...

459
00:29:39.194 --> 00:29:41.402
[applause]

460
00:29:41.488 --> 00:29:46.108
♪♪

461
00:30:00.048 --> 00:30:03.166
(VO) Senator Escobar is
denied entry the first day he

462
00:30:03.260 --> 00:30:05.923
attends Congress.
Why? Because he smuggles

463
00:30:06.013 --> 00:30:09.427
forty tons of cocaine a
year into the United States?

464
00:30:09.516 --> 00:30:10.677
No.

465
00:30:10.767 --> 00:30:12.554
(House Official) I'm sorry,
sir, but a tie is required

466
00:30:12.644 --> 00:30:13.885
to enter our chamber.

467
00:30:29.494 --> 00:30:31.326
(VO) That's my country for you.

468
00:30:31.413 --> 00:30:34.076
♪♪

469
00:30:44.384 --> 00:30:46.717
What are you doing
looking through my bag?

470
00:30:47.304 --> 00:30:49.967
That's not where you'll
find a picture of my lover.

471
00:30:53.727 --> 00:30:54.843
What's that?

472
00:30:54.936 --> 00:30:57.895
It's a surprise,
surprise for you.

473
00:30:57.981 --> 00:31:00.769
Pablo, take that money
out of my bag right now!

474
00:31:00.859 --> 00:31:01.690
Why?

475
00:31:01.777 --> 00:31:03.109
You're not going to
put me in danger!

476
00:31:03.195 --> 00:31:05.187
I have nothing to do
with your business, okay?

477
00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:08.364
It's a gift for you, Virginia.
This is for you to enjoy it.

478
00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:09.816
A gift.

479
00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:10.900
This is a gift for me?

480
00:31:13.080 --> 00:31:15.072
But, Pablo, that's
a lot of money!

481
00:31:15.165 --> 00:31:16.451
I know, but don't worry.

482
00:31:16.541 --> 00:31:19.033
The American government doesn't
care how much you bring in, it

483
00:31:19.127 --> 00:31:20.914
only cares how
much you take out.

484
00:31:21.004 --> 00:31:23.121
So you can declare it all
when you get to customs.

485
00:31:23.215 --> 00:31:25.377
But it's too much!
I cannot accept it.

486
00:31:25.467 --> 00:31:26.708
Look, it doesn't even fit.

487
00:31:26.802 --> 00:31:27.792
That's the problem,
it doesn't fit.

488
00:31:27.886 --> 00:31:29.218
We have to take out the clothes.

489
00:31:29.304 --> 00:31:30.886
You can buy new ones there, see?

490
00:31:30.972 --> 00:31:32.884
Take them all out.
Take them all out.

491
00:31:32.974 --> 00:31:35.182
But you have to spend all the
money, you can't bring anything

492
00:31:35.268 --> 00:31:36.179
back with you, Virginia.

493
00:31:37.813 --> 00:31:40.226
All my life waiting
to hear those words!

494
00:31:49.408 --> 00:31:52.025
(VO) Colombians don't
turn on their TVs to see me,

495
00:31:52.119 --> 00:31:53.826
but what I'm wearing.

496
00:31:54.830 --> 00:31:57.994
Pablo is aware of this, and he
takes care of all my needs.

497
00:32:08.552 --> 00:32:12.262
(Escobar) This is called
coca paste. And the poorest

498
00:32:12.347 --> 00:32:15.090
drug addicts mix it with
gasoline and call it bazook.

499
00:32:15.934 --> 00:32:17.596
This crap will fry your brain.

500
00:32:17.686 --> 00:32:18.642
There's nothing
worse than this.

501
00:32:22.107 --> 00:32:26.477
Now, when you cook it, you
get this little white powder

502
00:32:26.570 --> 00:32:28.232
but it's the same shit.

503
00:32:28.321 --> 00:32:30.563
We work with this, eh?

504
00:32:30.657 --> 00:32:32.569
But we do not take it here.

505
00:32:34.161 --> 00:32:35.948
Have you heard of Nancy Reagan?

506
00:32:36.872 --> 00:32:38.238
No?

507
00:32:38.331 --> 00:32:40.823
She's a very important lady and
she says that if anybody offers

508
00:32:40.917 --> 00:32:43.159
you this stuff, you just say no.

509
00:32:43.253 --> 00:32:45.290
You're going to
listen to that lady.

510
