[girl screams]

1019
01:08:42.827 --> 01:08:44.068
[explosion]

1020
01:08:46.789 --> 01:08:48.280
[sobbing]

1021
01:08:56.424 --> 01:08:58.211
(Monje) Listen,
I need to reach Pablo.

1022
01:08:58.301 --> 01:09:00.338
Our people in Miami are
getting out of line.

1023
01:09:00.428 --> 01:09:03.171
The routes are falling apart,
and the Cali Cartel is getting

1024
01:09:03.264 --> 01:09:05.881
our territory!
We can't finance this war

1025
01:09:05.975 --> 01:09:08.342
if the business stops
working, you understand?

1026
01:09:16.903 --> 01:09:18.394
I don't want you to kill them.

1027
01:09:18.488 --> 01:09:19.649
They're our link up there.

1028
01:09:19.739 --> 01:09:20.900
I just want you to find Pablo.

1029
01:09:20.990 --> 01:09:22.731
Is that so difficult
to understand to you?

1030
01:09:22.825 --> 01:09:23.941
[gun shot]

1031
01:09:27.372 --> 01:09:30.240
(VO) Monje's death
meant the fall of the

1032
01:09:30.333 --> 01:09:31.869
cartel's financial wing.

1033
01:09:39.008 --> 01:09:42.046
Garza's death meant the
fall of the toughest wing.

1034
01:09:44.931 --> 01:09:46.638
[rapid gun fire]

1035
01:09:54.732 --> 01:09:56.815
Pablo loses his strong men.

1036
01:09:57.694 --> 01:10:00.186
From this point on,
he can only run.

1037
01:10:00.738 --> 01:10:03.321
(Escobar) For years we have
called for peace, but the only

1038
01:10:03.408 --> 01:10:06.025
response we've gotten has
been official and systemic

1039
01:10:06.119 --> 01:10:09.738
persecution against our
families and organizations.

1040
01:10:09.831 --> 01:10:13.290
KEEP HIM ON THE LINE That's why I declare
full out war on the government and the

1041
01:10:13.376 --> 01:10:14.833
political establishment.

1042
01:10:14.919 --> 01:10:17.411
If they make me run,
I make them run too.

1043
01:10:17.880 --> 01:10:20.247
Terrorism is the atomic
bomb of the poor.

1044
01:10:20.341 --> 01:10:22.128
ONE MORE MINUTE
We're not using lead anymore.

1045
01:10:22.218 --> 01:10:25.461
From now on, we're using
dynamite, understand?

1046
01:10:26.222 --> 01:10:30.136
(Announcer) And how do we know
that you are really Pablo

1047
01:10:30.226 --> 01:10:34.641
Escobar Gaviria and not someone
else pretending to be him?

1048
01:10:34.731 --> 01:10:36.472
That is very easy.

1049
01:10:36.566 --> 01:10:38.933
I will prove it to you by
killing you and your family

1050
01:10:39.026 --> 01:10:41.393
tonight, and blowing
up your radio station.

1051
01:10:41.487 --> 01:10:43.319
What do you think?
Would that be enough?

1052
01:10:43.406 --> 01:10:44.942
Hey!

1053
01:10:46.242 --> 01:10:47.949
(Producer) You're a celebrity
in your country, Virginia.

1054
01:10:48.035 --> 01:10:51.199
What's so appealing about coming
to Miami to host a TV show?

1055
01:10:53.082 --> 01:10:56.371
Well... I don't really

1056
01:10:56.461 --> 01:10:58.748
think I have anything
else to prove in Colombia.

1057
01:10:59.505 --> 01:11:00.666
No?

1058
01:11:01.799 --> 01:11:07.045
But I guess what appeals
to me is the challenge,

1059
01:11:07.138 --> 01:11:10.131
the excitement
of a new adventure.

1060
01:11:12.518 --> 01:11:16.228
Also, there are some very
attractive men in this

1061
01:11:16.314 --> 01:11:17.805
part of the world.

1062
01:11:19.192 --> 01:11:21.434
Tell us, Virginia, what's
the last show you hosted on

1063
01:11:21.527 --> 01:11:22.859
Colombian TV?

1064
01:11:33.539 --> 01:11:34.950
(Agent) How you doing?

1065
01:11:35.041 --> 01:11:36.248
FBI.

1066
01:11:36.334 --> 01:11:38.826
Mind if we take a
look at your passport?

1067
01:11:46.803 --> 01:11:48.669
You carry any money?

1068
01:11:49.305 --> 01:11:52.093
My ex isn't using
me as a mule, yet.

1069
01:11:54.352 --> 01:11:55.468
Okay.

1070
01:11:55.978 --> 01:11:57.810
(Woman Reacting) Oh, my God!

1071
01:12:07.365 --> 01:12:08.321
What happened?

1072
01:12:08.407 --> 01:12:10.649
I'm sorry, they just
closed Bogota Airport.

1073
01:12:10.743 --> 01:12:11.733
Why?

1074
01:12:11.828 --> 01:12:12.818
I'll call you back.

1075
01:12:12.912 --> 01:12:15.029
An Avianca plane
exploded in midflight.

1076
01:12:15.706 --> 01:12:16.867
[woman sobbing]

1077
01:12:28.052 --> 01:12:31.090
(VO) After the first bombs,
the country asked the government

1078
01:12:31.180 --> 01:12:32.887
to give Pablo hell.

1079
01:12:55.288 --> 01:12:58.247
(VO) After a dozen bombs,
the country begs the government

1080
01:12:58.332 --> 01:13:00.790
to give Pablo what he wants.

1081
01:13:00.877 --> 01:13:02.914
[explosion, screams]

1082
01:13:18.561 --> 01:13:19.927
Pablo!

1083
01:13:20.438 --> 01:13:23.181
[sirens wailing]

1084
01:13:35.828 --> 01:13:37.194
(Santos) Newell.

1085
01:13:39.040 --> 01:13:41.407
There was a Newell in
my graduating class.

1086
01:13:41.959 --> 01:13:43.996
You think it could be him?

1087
01:13:44.670 --> 01:13:45.706
What is it?

1088
01:13:45.796 --> 01:13:48.038
List of victims on
the Avianca flight.

1089
01:13:48.633 --> 01:13:51.216
107 people on board.

1090
01:13:51.302 --> 01:13:52.838
They just sent it.

1091
01:13:55.181 --> 01:13:57.764
Robin Newell and
Catherine Gilmore.

1092
01:13:57.850 --> 01:14:00.183
35, 32 years old.

1093
01:14:00.770 --> 01:14:02.352
Married.

1094
01:14:11.072 --> 01:14:11.858
(Secretary) Sir?

1095
01:14:11.948 --> 01:14:13.359
Sir, wait.

1096
01:14:14.659 --> 01:14:17.743
Ambassador, there were two
Americans on the Avianca flight.

1097
01:14:17.828 --> 01:14:22.744
So, listen, directive 12.333
authorizes military operations

1098
01:14:22.833 --> 01:14:25.166
in foreign countries to
guarantee the security of

1099
01:14:25.252 --> 01:14:27.039
American citizens...
(Williams) Thank you, Sarah.

1100
01:14:27.129 --> 01:14:29.963
Agent Shepard, I'm sure
you know Mr. Velarde.

1101
01:14:30.049 --> 01:14:32.041
He's also the man in charge
of negotiating the surrender

1102
01:14:32.134 --> 01:14:33.466
of Pablo Escobar.

1103
01:14:33.552 --> 01:14:35.589
This is Mr. Castro.

1104
01:14:35.680 --> 01:14:38.468
He's Mr. Escobar's
legal representative.

1105
01:14:40.059 --> 01:14:43.018
He's agreed to turn himself
in to the authorities.

1106
01:14:45.022 --> 01:14:46.354
In exchange for what?

1107
01:14:51.904 --> 01:14:54.942
By revoking the Extradition
Treaty, our judges and

1108
01:14:55.032 --> 01:14:59.151
magistrates have taught the
world a lesson in sovereignty,

1109
01:14:59.245 --> 01:15:01.111
independence and patriotism.

1110
01:15:01.497 --> 01:15:03.534
After years of persecution...

1111
01:15:03.624 --> 01:15:06.742
♪♪

1112
01:15:54.717 --> 01:15:58.006
(VO) Pablo adds one last
condition to his surrender.

1113
01:15:58.888 --> 01:16:00.971
He provides the prison.

1114
01:16:01.724 --> 01:16:05.308
♪♪

1115
01:16:05.394 --> 01:16:07.807
(Escobar)
It is very pretty, isn't it?

1116
01:16:17.698 --> 01:16:21.157
(VO) He cedes the property to
the municipality through a front

1117
01:16:21.243 --> 01:16:23.576
man so they can build it there.

1118
01:16:43.265 --> 01:16:45.097
Everyone's here
but the President.

1119
01:16:45.184 --> 01:16:46.595
He couldn't make it.

1120
01:16:46.685 --> 01:16:48.096
Scheduling problems.

1121
01:16:51.774 --> 01:16:54.812
(VO) Without the threat of
extradition hanging over him

1122
01:16:54.902 --> 01:16:57.565
Pablo needs a safe place to
reorganize his business.

1123
01:17:01.534 --> 01:17:04.242
(VO) And the government
provides him with one.

1124
01:17:06.122 --> 01:17:08.535
(Santoro) The Conception
and Norman Key routes are

1125
01:17:08.624 --> 01:17:12.334
working again. The Fany is
at almost one hundred percent.

1126
01:17:12.419 --> 01:17:15.787
We have 250 planes in service

1127
01:17:15.881 --> 01:17:18.965
and 30 Pipers still
immobilized in Santamarca.

1128
01:17:19.051 --> 01:17:22.886
Are you talking to the number
two at the Aviation Authority?

1129
01:17:22.972 --> 01:17:25.089
Talk to him, he's a brother.
If he doesn't want to play

1130
01:17:25.182 --> 01:17:27.094
ball you bring him
here and I talk to him.

1131
01:17:31.021 --> 01:17:35.516
So, for everyone who is still
outside nobody moves a gram

1132
01:17:35.609 --> 01:17:37.225
without me knowing it.

1133
01:17:37.319 --> 01:17:39.106
Nobody. Understood?

1134
01:17:39.196 --> 01:17:42.610
They have to pay the
taxes that they owe me.

1135
01:17:42.700 --> 01:17:43.781
That's 20 percent.

1136
01:17:43.868 --> 01:17:46.076
...20 percent?
...20 percent.

1137
01:17:46.162 --> 01:17:48.074
They won't like that, Pablo.

1138
01:17:48.164 --> 01:17:50.372
The Cali people are
asking for five percent.

1139
01:17:50.457 --> 01:17:53.495
Jesus, everyone will
go to them and that's OK.

1140
01:17:53.586 --> 01:17:56.169
How do you know that?
Have you talked to them?

1141
01:18:07.850 --> 01:18:10.593
You prefer those
pussies from Cali,

1142
01:18:10.686 --> 01:18:12.268
go to them and try your luck.

1143
01:18:12.354 --> 01:18:16.064
I came up with the routes, I
took out extradition all by

1144
01:18:16.150 --> 01:18:17.812
myself so you can keep working.

1145
01:18:17.902 --> 01:18:20.895
So make everybody knows that the
one who hasn't paid with cash,

1146
01:18:20.988 --> 01:18:23.401
merchandise or properties
will pay with his life.

1147
01:18:29.413 --> 01:18:30.449
What's next?

1148
01:18:30.539 --> 01:18:32.451
♪♪

1149
01:18:32.541 --> 01:18:35.204
(VO) Soccer players from the
professional league come to

1150
01:18:35.294 --> 01:18:36.910
play with the traffickers.

1151
01:18:37.004 --> 01:18:40.088
♪♪

1152
01:18:48.432 --> 01:18:51.596
(VO) And the match isn't
over until the Patrón wins.

1153
01:18:55.314 --> 01:18:56.771
[cheering]

1154
01:18:59.151 --> 01:19:02.189
The social workers have arrived!

1155
01:19:02.279 --> 01:19:05.647
♪♪

1156
01:19:41.235 --> 01:19:43.522
(VO) Sundays are
saved for family.

1157
01:20:09.471 --> 01:20:12.305
(Manuela) Why don't you
live at home with us, Daddy?

1158
01:20:14.560 --> 01:20:17.143
Because I work here, Princess.

1159
01:20:17.855 --> 01:20:20.063
My princess.

1160
01:20:22.401 --> 01:20:24.768
This is my castle. I...

1161
01:20:25.654 --> 01:20:27.862
Do you see those
towers there?

1162
01:20:27.948 --> 01:20:29.314
Those are my towers.

1163
01:20:30.200 --> 01:20:32.817
I am a king, and
king has castles.

1164
01:20:34.371 --> 01:20:37.614
And that's why
you are a princess,

1165
01:20:37.708 --> 01:20:39.119
because you are my daughter.

1166
01:20:39.752 --> 01:20:40.959
But there are guards.

1167
01:20:41.045 --> 01:20:42.786
Yes, of course there are.

1168
01:20:42.880 --> 01:20:44.587
They are here to protect me.

1169
01:20:46.759 --> 01:20:50.469
Mommy says you can't leave,
and she cries all the time.

1170
01:20:51.347 --> 01:20:53.839
What do you mean I can't leave?

1171
01:20:55.601 --> 01:20:56.717
Who says that?

1172
01:20:56.810 --> 01:20:57.926
Mommy.

1173
01:21:02.775 --> 01:21:06.485
This is my castle.
I can come and go as I please.

1174
01:21:11.200 --> 01:21:12.736
You wanna see that?

1175
01:21:12.826 --> 01:21:16.069
You want to go out
for an ice cream?

1176
01:21:17.331 --> 01:21:22.247
Where is the place that the
big park near the church.

1177
01:21:22.336 --> 01:21:23.918
That's the one you like.

1178
01:21:25.964 --> 01:21:27.375
Let's go.

1179
01:21:27.841 --> 01:21:29.503
Let's go.

1180
01:21:33.889 --> 01:21:35.380
What did you have for lunch?

1181
01:21:36.058 --> 01:21:37.640
Good Lord.

1182
01:21:41.897 --> 01:21:43.058
Don't wait for us.

1183
01:21:43.148 --> 01:21:45.561
Manuela and I are going
out for an ice cream.

1184
01:21:45.651 --> 01:21:47.938
Pablito still has
his sense of humor.

1185
01:22:01.250 --> 01:22:03.492
Who's in charge of this castle?

1186
01:22:04.128 --> 01:22:05.744
Who's the boss here?

1187
01:22:06.422 --> 01:22:07.458
(Guard) You, Patrón.

1188
01:22:07.548 --> 01:22:09.756
Yeah, that's what I like
to hear. Open the door.

1189
01:22:09.842 --> 01:22:11.208
Open the door!

1190
01:22:12.136 --> 01:22:13.672
(Escobar) Open it.

1191
01:22:19.017 --> 01:22:21.851
The king and his princess are
going out for an ice cream.

1192
01:22:21.937 --> 01:22:23.849
What flavor you want?
...Strawberry!

1193
01:22:23.939 --> 01:22:27.103
Strawberry!
The princess has a craving!

1194
01:22:27.776 --> 01:22:30.564
If you dare to stop us, the
king will cut your heads off.

1195
01:22:30.654 --> 01:22:32.361
Open the door.
Open the door.

1196
01:22:41.540 --> 01:22:42.576
Our carriage is waiting for us.

1197
01:22:44.418 --> 01:22:45.078
Give me the keys.

1198
01:22:45.669 --> 01:22:47.160
Give me the keys, man.

1199
01:22:47.254 --> 01:22:49.667
The king is asking for
the keys of the car.

1200
01:22:49.756 --> 01:22:51.497
Give me the keys.
Give me the keys, man!

1201
01:23:13.530 --> 01:23:15.066
(Victoria) Pablo!

1202
01:23:19.578 --> 01:23:20.568
Pablo!

1203
01:23:40.307 --> 01:23:43.425
I forgot to tell you,
my princess, that...

1204
01:23:44.561 --> 01:23:47.599
I made them bring
the best ice cream,

1205
01:23:47.689 --> 01:23:51.683
strawberry ice cream
of the world here for you.

1206
01:23:54.238 --> 01:23:57.857
Strawberry ice cream just made
with ice from the North Pole

1207
01:23:57.950 --> 01:24:01.318
which is especially for
my daughter my princess,

1208
01:24:01.411 --> 01:24:02.697
especially!

1209
01:24:02.788 --> 01:24:04.404
The best one in the world!

1210
01:24:04.498 --> 01:24:05.739
For you.

1211
01:24:05.832 --> 01:24:06.913
(Manuela) Really?

1212
01:24:08.585 --> 01:24:11.123
Have you heard of the strawberry
icebergs in the North Pole?

1213
01:24:11.213 --> 01:24:12.249
They're very famous.

1214
01:24:12.339 --> 01:24:14.797
(VO) Not only has
the media banned me.

1215
01:24:14.883 --> 01:24:18.627
My advertising contracts are
also cancelled which forces me

1216
01:24:18.720 --> 01:24:21.212
to sell my home to pay my debts.

1217
01:24:22.099 --> 01:24:23.215
Be careful with that!

1218
01:24:24.017 --> 01:24:27.226
What you just moved with your
foot is a very expensive piece

1219
01:24:27.312 --> 01:24:28.928
of Indonesian art.

1220
01:24:29.022 --> 01:24:31.435
I'm not asking you
to use your head.

1221
01:24:31.942 --> 01:24:34.150
Using your hands will be enough.

1222
01:24:35.821 --> 01:24:38.905
(VO) I rent an apartment at El
Nogal where a former First Lady

1223
01:24:38.991 --> 01:24:42.780
lives, hoping her bodyguards
will keep an eye on me as well.

1224
01:24:44.871 --> 01:24:46.157
How are you boys?

1225
01:24:46.999 --> 01:24:48.786
(Man) Fine, thanks.

1226
01:24:51.461 --> 01:24:54.078
(VO) And I get a break
from the telephone threats.

1227
01:24:58.302 --> 01:24:59.383
(Technician) All set, ma'am.

1228
01:25:01.179 --> 01:25:02.715
[phone rings]

1229
01:25:05.350 --> 01:25:07.137
Wasn't it a new number?

1230
01:25:07.978 --> 01:25:09.890
(VO) But not for long.

1231
01:25:50.646 --> 01:25:51.636
[door opens]

1232
01:25:56.985 --> 01:25:58.567
Nice hotel!

1233
01:25:59.905 --> 01:26:01.521
How's our book going?

1234
01:26:01.615 --> 01:26:02.901
What book?

1235
01:26:02.991 --> 01:26:04.573
Who would want to
read a book about you?

1236
01:26:04.660 --> 01:26:05.946
I have my admirers.

1237
01:26:06.036 --> 01:26:08.449
Your admirers can't
read, they're too young.

1238
01:26:08.538 --> 01:26:10.530
That's true.
That's one of their virtues.

1239
01:26:10.624 --> 01:26:12.411
You know that I left
a meeting to see you,

1240
01:26:12.501 --> 01:26:14.208
so, what do you want? Tell me.

1241
01:26:17.964 --> 01:26:20.627
I need to know if I'm safe.

1242
01:26:21.426 --> 01:26:23.463
And how would I know that?

1243
01:26:23.553 --> 01:26:25.260
No one is safe in this country.

1244
01:26:25.347 --> 01:26:28.556
As far as you're
concerned, can I feel safe?

1245
01:26:30.435 --> 01:26:31.892
No!

1246
01:26:31.978 --> 01:26:35.016
Nobody will kill their own
biographer, don't worry.

1247
01:26:35.107 --> 01:26:36.814
Relax.

1248
01:26:38.026 --> 01:26:39.233
What else?

1249
01:26:42.531 --> 01:26:43.817
Oh, Pablo.

1250
01:26:45.075 --> 01:26:47.988
You can't imagine how
terrifying my life has become.

1251
01:26:48.954 --> 01:26:50.616
My phone won't stop ringing.

1252
01:26:50.706 --> 01:26:53.198
Threats, every day,
threats. You have an army

1253
01:26:53.291 --> 01:26:56.034
of men to protect you,
but who protects me?

1254
01:26:56.128 --> 01:26:57.710
What about me?

1255
01:26:58.547 --> 01:26:59.958
What can I do?

1256
01:27:03.802 --> 01:27:07.637
I need you to tell everyone
we are not together anymore.

1257
01:27:10.934 --> 01:27:12.675
You're breaking my heart.

1258
01:27:13.854 --> 01:27:16.141
After all that
I've done for you.

1259
01:27:16.898 --> 01:27:19.641
What have you done for me?
Nothing!

1260
01:27:19.735 --> 01:27:21.977
I already had a
career when I met you.

1261
01:27:22.070 --> 01:27:23.311
Don't forget that.

1262
01:27:23.405 --> 01:27:26.398
And I'm the only woman who has
loved you without expecting

1263
01:27:26.491 --> 01:27:29.154
anything in return and
that includes your wife.

1264
01:27:29.244 --> 01:27:30.735
No, no, no, no, no.

1265
01:27:30.829 --> 01:27:32.991
Don't you ever dare
to compare to my wife.

1266
01:27:33.081 --> 01:27:34.993
Don't even put the name
of Victoria on your lips.

1267
01:27:35.083 --> 01:27:36.745
She was with me when
I didn't have a peso.

1268
01:27:36.835 --> 01:27:38.576
Would you have
noticed me back then?

1269
01:27:38.670 --> 01:27:41.378
With no planes and no trips
and no shopping in New York?

1270
01:27:41.465 --> 01:27:44.253
Would you have?
No, tell me, would you?

1271
01:27:44.760 --> 01:27:45.841
I don't think so.

1272
01:27:47.387 --> 01:27:49.299
I'm broke, Pablo!

1273
01:27:49.389 --> 01:27:52.177
I'm broke! My career
is over because of you!

1274
01:27:52.267 --> 01:27:54.975
Nobody will hire me
anymore because of you!

1275
01:27:55.061 --> 01:27:56.643
So you need to help me!

1276
01:27:56.730 --> 01:27:58.062
How? What do you need?

1277
01:27:58.148 --> 01:27:59.764
Tell me.

1278
01:28:01.818 --> 01:28:04.151
What do you need, Virginia?

1279
01:28:06.323 --> 01:28:08.906
80 thousand dollars
to go to Europe.

1280
01:28:10.869 --> 01:28:12.906
80 thousand dollars.

1281
01:28:12.996 --> 01:28:14.237
That's a lot of money.

1282
01:28:15.624 --> 01:28:17.536
80 thousand dollars.

1283
01:28:17.626 --> 01:28:19.367
I don't have that money.

1284
01:28:20.420 --> 01:28:21.752
No, I don't.

1285
01:28:21.838 --> 01:28:24.706
And you are my biographer,
you have to stay here.

1286
01:28:26.051 --> 01:28:27.167
[gasp]

1287
01:28:31.681 --> 01:28:33.388
I've seen things, Pablo.

1288
01:28:33.475 --> 01:28:34.932
I've seen things.

1289
01:28:35.018 --> 01:28:36.509
While I was with you.

1290
01:28:36.603 --> 01:28:37.719
You've seen what?

1291
01:28:37.813 --> 01:28:40.055
Things that implicate
a lot of people!

1292
01:28:40.148 --> 01:28:42.606
If I wanted to talk!
[laughs]

1293
01:28:47.447 --> 01:28:48.733
If you what?

1294
01:28:50.158 --> 01:28:51.114
No, no, no, no!

1295
01:28:51.201 --> 01:28:53.443
No, I never expected
this from you. Really.

1296
01:28:53.537 --> 01:28:55.529
My God, that's not what I mean!

1297
01:28:55.622 --> 01:28:57.955
Pablo, I would never betray you!

1298
01:28:58.708 --> 01:29:00.324
It's just that I'm desperate!

1299
01:29:00.418 --> 01:29:02.751
I don't even know what
I'm saying anymore!

1300
01:29:03.255 --> 01:29:05.212
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1301
01:29:08.385 --> 01:29:09.842
Don't worry.

1302
01:29:10.303 --> 01:29:12.716
Don't worry, I will
take care of you.

1303
01:29:12.806 --> 01:29:14.388
I will protect you.

1304
01:29:14.474 --> 01:29:16.511
I'll make sure you
have a long life.

1305
01:29:19.563 --> 01:29:20.974
You want to know what?

1306
01:29:21.731 --> 01:29:23.848
I have bad news for you.

1307
01:29:25.569 --> 01:29:27.731
Nobody will get near you
because they will be afraid

1308
01:29:27.821 --> 01:29:29.107
that I will kill them.

1309
01:29:29.197 --> 01:29:32.235
So your life is going
to be full of shit.

1310
01:29:37.706 --> 01:29:39.117
[whimpering]

1311
01:29:51.803 --> 01:29:53.214
[door slams]

1312
01:29:53.305 --> 01:29:55.297
[sobs]

1313
01:30:03.899 --> 01:30:07.859
♪♪

1314
01:30:13.199 --> 01:30:14.531
(Escobar) Peladito.

1315
01:30:15.327 --> 01:30:15.908
[laughs]

1316
01:30:18.038 --> 01:30:20.496
(Santoro) The things are
getting rough out there, man.

1317
01:30:22.417 --> 01:30:24.750
Business, business
isn't good, man.

1318
01:30:24.836 --> 01:30:27.044
No, they're not good, no.

1319
01:30:34.763 --> 01:30:39.975
One question the Fany route
moves, what, 10 kilos a month?

1320
01:30:40.477 --> 01:30:41.388
Yeah.

1321
01:30:42.646 --> 01:30:46.105
And you pay me,
what 50 thousand?

1322
01:30:46.441 --> 01:30:47.181
50 thousand?

1323
01:30:48.985 --> 01:30:51.352
The Fany route
failed twice this month.

1324
01:30:51.446 --> 01:30:54.029
We lost two 600... kilo shipments.

1325
01:30:54.115 --> 01:30:58.485
We have to pay the owners,
hire lawyers for the pilots.

1326
01:30:59.079 --> 01:31:02.322
Yeah, yeah, but the
deal was 250, no?

1327
01:31:02.415 --> 01:31:03.951
I gave you that route, remember?

1328
01:31:08.546 --> 01:31:10.583
250 is impossible, Pablo.

1329
01:31:10.674 --> 01:31:12.540
Is impossible, I mean it.

1330
01:31:20.684 --> 01:31:22.266
Trust us.

1331
01:31:22.352 --> 01:31:24.344
We are your partners,
you son of a bitch.

1332
01:31:24.437 --> 01:31:25.973
We've been together
from the start.

1333
01:31:29.734 --> 01:31:31.521
Well, we're not
in this together.

1334
01:31:31.611 --> 01:31:32.601
I'm here and you're out.

1335
01:31:32.696 --> 01:31:34.153
Yeah, we know that, Pablo.

1336
01:31:37.826 --> 01:31:41.194
But you have to pay me the tax.
So...

1337
01:31:44.833 --> 01:31:45.994
You have to.

1338
01:31:47.127 --> 01:31:49.870
Either you pay it, or
I double it right now.

1339
01:31:54.634 --> 01:31:56.751
We have to discuss it
with the other families.

1340
01:31:59.264 --> 01:32:01.176
Business has changed a lot.

1341
01:32:01.266 --> 01:32:03.758
Things aren't the same
they used to be anymore.

1342
01:32:03.852 --> 01:32:05.343
50 thousand should be enough.

1343
01:32:11.985 --> 01:32:13.601
50 thousand should be enough.

1344
01:32:16.031 --> 01:32:20.492
So you come here to
sit down in front of me

1345
01:32:20.577 --> 01:32:23.786
with that gold and
those fancy clothes.

1346
01:32:26.207 --> 01:32:28.620
You're all getting rich
out there, while I am here.

1347
01:32:28.710 --> 01:32:29.700
No, no, no, Pablo.

1348
01:32:29.794 --> 01:32:31.626
And then you're flirting
with the Cali people.

1349
01:32:31.713 --> 01:32:33.500
And to top it off, you
don't want even to pay me.

1350
01:32:44.392 --> 01:32:48.056
♪♪

1351
01:33:02.452 --> 01:33:04.284
[screaming]

1352
01:33:05.121 --> 01:33:06.953
No, no, don't complain.

1353
01:33:07.040 --> 01:33:08.406
Don't complain.
You are already dead.

1354
01:33:08.500 --> 01:33:09.286
This is just a formality.

1355
01:33:16.591 --> 01:33:18.878
This way your families can
put the pieces back together.

1356
01:33:23.181 --> 01:33:25.343
[chainsaw roaring]

1357
01:33:26.601 --> 01:33:30.811
♪♪

1358
01:33:35.860 --> 01:33:38.853
(VO) The murders at La Catedral
reached the media and make the

1359
01:33:38.947 --> 01:33:40.688
government an accomplice.

1360
01:33:41.157 --> 01:33:42.193
[explosion]

1361
01:33:42.283 --> 01:33:44.525
Its credibility is at stake.

1362
01:33:45.120 --> 01:33:48.113
They decide to transfer
Pablo to a military prison.

1363
01:34:10.395 --> 01:34:12.808
(VO) The fence of
the prison was electric

1364
01:34:13.565 --> 01:34:15.807
but the switch
was in Pablo's room.

1365
01:34:28.997 --> 01:34:31.455
(La Plaga) Our people are
turning on us, Patrón.

1366
01:34:32.876 --> 01:34:35.664
Apparently, they're
thinking, if he did that to

1367
01:34:35.753 --> 01:34:38.666
Santoro and Hermosilla,
what will he do to us?

1368
01:34:42.385 --> 01:34:44.502
Running like chickens
straight to Cali.

1369
01:34:50.727 --> 01:34:53.265
What, do you think
that was a mistake?

1370
01:34:57.901 --> 01:34:59.437
(VO) Sure it was.

1371
01:35:03.364 --> 01:35:06.573
Pablo's ex... associates
cooperate with the government

1372
01:35:06.659 --> 01:35:08.651
in exchange for having
their records cleared.

1373
01:35:12.540 --> 01:35:15.408
Dozens of narcos willing
to fight hinn are released.

1374
01:35:19.964 --> 01:35:20.954
(Ignacio Castro)
To the airport.

1375
01:35:28.056 --> 01:35:29.592
Son, say goodbye.

1376
01:35:29.682 --> 01:35:32.265
This is not a country,
it's a mass grave.

1377
01:35:35.688 --> 01:35:36.599
[yelp]

1378
01:35:37.774 --> 01:35:38.855
Hey hey hey!

1379
01:35:38.942 --> 01:35:41.059
Who are you?
What the fuck do you want?

1380
01:35:41.402 --> 01:35:42.518
[crack]

1381
01:35:46.199 --> 01:35:47.610
[squealing tires]

1382
01:35:48.076 --> 01:35:51.035
(VO) Pablo's enemies,
members of rival cartels,

1383
01:35:51.120 --> 01:35:54.033
and paramilitary groups
together with government

1384
01:35:54.123 --> 01:35:58.458
security forces supported by
the DEA and the CIA formed

1385
01:35:58.544 --> 01:36:02.037
the most lethal hunting
party of all time.

1386
01:36:13.601 --> 01:36:16.765
(VO) The bodies of Pablo's
lawyers, hitnnen, accountants,

1387
01:36:16.854 --> 01:36:20.143
and family appear
scattered all over Medellin.

1388
01:36:35.748 --> 01:36:36.909
[screams]

1389
01:36:46.426 --> 01:36:50.340
(VO) Anyone who's ever been
close to him becomes a target.

1390
01:37:03.026 --> 01:37:04.062
[door buzzer]

1391
01:37:09.615 --> 01:37:10.981
(Buyer) Good morning.
Can I help you?

1392
01:37:11.075 --> 01:37:12.282
Good morning.

1393
01:37:17.790 --> 01:37:20.328
These belonged to
European royalty.

1394
01:37:22.462 --> 01:37:23.873
And these earrings.

1395
01:37:26.341 --> 01:37:28.128
If you give me a good
price, I bring you more.

1396
01:37:28.217 --> 01:37:29.708
Okay. Let me have a look.

1397
01:37:31.679 --> 01:37:32.886
Exquisite.

1398
01:37:32.972 --> 01:37:34.088
[knocks on window]

1399
01:37:39.103 --> 01:37:40.514
Don't open the door.

1400
01:37:40.605 --> 01:37:42.062
...Do you know him?
...No.

1401
01:37:43.858 --> 01:37:44.564
Call the police.

1402
01:37:45.109 --> 01:37:46.316
Call the police.

1403
01:37:46.402 --> 01:37:47.358
[door buzzer]

1404
01:37:52.950 --> 01:37:54.157
Call the police!

1405
01:37:54.243 --> 01:37:55.199
[clanking]
...I'm sorry.

1406
01:37:55.286 --> 01:37:57.073
No! What are you doing?

1407
01:37:57.163 --> 01:37:58.745
I don't want to get in trouble.
Sorry.

1408
01:37:58.831 --> 01:38:01.790
Let me in! Let me in!
Let me in!

1409
01:38:01.876 --> 01:38:02.912
Let me in!

1410
01:38:05.546 --> 01:38:06.957
[muffled] Let me in!

1411
01:38:15.890 --> 01:38:17.552
No no nooo!!

1412
01:38:20.728 --> 01:38:22.560
[muffled gun fire]

1413
01:38:26.818 --> 01:38:29.481
[panicked screaming]

1414
01:38:33.741 --> 01:38:36.529
[wailing]

1415
01:38:48.089 --> 01:38:50.001
[car starts]

1416
01:39:03.855 --> 01:39:05.562
[panting]

1417
01:39:13.489 --> 01:39:17.199
♪♪

1418
01:39:41.601 --> 01:39:43.558
I'm going to be a star.

1419
01:39:44.687 --> 01:39:45.803
Look.

1420
01:39:47.899 --> 01:39:49.891
Victoria, do you hear that?

1421
01:39:49.984 --> 01:39:52.351
Manuela's gonna be a
star in a Christmas show.

1422
01:39:55.364 --> 01:39:57.105
Will you come and see me?

1423
01:39:58.701 --> 01:40:00.237
Yes, I will.

1424
01:40:01.162 --> 01:40:03.370
Mom made me a shiny costume.

1425
01:40:07.460 --> 01:40:09.622
I am sure you're
beautiful in it.

1426
01:40:14.383 --> 01:40:16.090
Don't cry. Don't cry.

1427
01:40:19.555 --> 01:40:20.887
She won't be in the show.

1428
01:40:20.973 --> 01:40:21.884
What?

1429
01:40:22.683 --> 01:40:23.799
Why?

1430
01:40:25.228 --> 01:40:27.641
The parents of the other
children objected.

1431
01:40:27.730 --> 01:40:29.312
They held an assembly.

1432
01:40:30.066 --> 01:40:31.432
She doesn't know yet.

1433
01:40:31.526 --> 01:40:32.312
Why?

1434
01:40:34.237 --> 01:40:35.398
Why?

1435
01:40:36.364 --> 01:40:38.606
Because they're afraid your
enemies will blow up the school,

1436
01:40:38.699 --> 01:40:39.906
Pablo, that's why.

1437
01:40:39.992 --> 01:40:40.903
They are scared.

1438
01:40:51.420 --> 01:40:52.536
Give me your hand.

1439
01:40:54.632 --> 01:40:57.500
I need you to take the kids,

1440
01:40:57.593 --> 01:41:00.552
get in a plane and get
out of this country.

1441
01:41:01.514 --> 01:41:03.927
It's getting very
dangerous for you here.

1442
01:41:05.184 --> 01:41:06.550
You can't stay here.

1443
01:41:06.644 --> 01:41:07.805
You can't.

1444
01:41:08.896 --> 01:41:12.936
So, once you leave I
can take care of things.

1445
01:41:15.152 --> 01:41:17.235
You didn't keep
your promise, Pablo.

1446
01:41:18.239 --> 01:41:20.196
You promised me
everything would be fine.

1447
01:41:20.283 --> 01:41:21.239
I know.

1448
01:41:21.325 --> 01:41:23.066
That my children would
have a normal life.

1449
01:41:23.911 --> 01:41:26.198
Does this seem like
a normal life to you?

1450
01:41:35.923 --> 01:41:36.788
[door closes]

1451
01:41:53.566 --> 01:41:56.024
There's a woman out here,
she wants to talk to you.

1452
01:41:56.110 --> 01:41:57.146
What's her name?

1453
01:41:57.236 --> 01:41:59.398
I don't know. She got
mad at me when I asked.

1454
01:42:01.073 --> 01:42:02.780
Says she's famous around here.

1455
01:42:23.429 --> 01:42:26.297
He needs to get his
family out of the country.

1456
01:42:26.390 --> 01:42:28.347
They cannot stay here.
They would reach them

1457
01:42:28.434 --> 01:42:30.551
in America, so they
have to go to Europe.

1458
01:42:30.645 --> 01:42:33.433
And as soon as they are out,
he'll feel free to

1459
01:42:33.522 --> 01:42:36.185
destroy everything.
So you cannot let them leave.

1460
01:42:36.901 --> 01:42:39.609
As long as they are here, he'll
be busy trying to protect them.

1461
01:42:40.780 --> 01:42:42.396
You better trust me.

1462
01:42:42.490 --> 01:42:43.731
You can't let them leave.

1463
01:42:43.824 --> 01:42:47.033
This is his weak spot, his
family, his family, his family.

1464
01:42:47.119 --> 01:42:49.486
It's all he cares
about, nothing else.

1465
01:42:50.539 --> 01:42:53.247
And you know that
firsthand, don't you?

1466
01:42:53.334 --> 01:42:55.951
No you have no idea.

1467
01:42:56.671 --> 01:42:58.879
(Velarde) We can't do that.

1468
01:42:59.840 --> 01:43:02.503
The Attorney General is the one
getting them out of the country.

1469
01:43:02.593 --> 01:43:03.709
They made a deal.

1470
01:43:03.803 --> 01:43:06.341
Once they're out, Pablo
Escobar will turn himself in.

1471
01:43:06.430 --> 01:43:07.796
Break your word.

1472
01:43:07.890 --> 01:43:10.052
Let's put some pressure
on the German Chancellor.

1473
01:43:10.142 --> 01:43:13.260
They land in Cologne
in two hours.

1474
01:43:13.354 --> 01:43:15.141
Do not let them
get off that plane.

1475
01:43:15.231 --> 01:43:17.518
There's no legal reason they
can't travel to Germany.

1476
01:43:17.608 --> 01:43:18.769
Bring them back.

1477
01:43:18.859 --> 01:43:21.693
The family is bait.
We need them alive and at home.

1478
01:43:21.779 --> 01:43:23.771
Put them someplace,
and we sit and we wait.

1479
01:43:23.864 --> 01:43:26.481
Pablo will try to
talk to them, right?

1480
01:43:26.575 --> 01:43:28.737
When that happens,
we'll be ready.

1481
01:43:33.582 --> 01:43:36.450
(Newscaster) Pablo Escobar
Gaviria's family was greeted by

1482
01:43:36.544 --> 01:43:39.662
a strong security presence
upon arrival in Bogota this

1483
01:43:39.755 --> 01:43:43.089
morning after being
denied entry into Germany.

1484
01:43:43.175 --> 01:43:45.963
The wife and the two children
of the couple were forced to

1485
01:43:46.053 --> 01:43:48.887
spend the night in Cologne's
airport, and later sent back

1486
01:43:48.973 --> 01:43:50.509
to Colombia on a regular...

1487
01:43:52.143 --> 01:43:53.600
They have taken
my family hostage!

1488
01:43:59.692 --> 01:44:02.526
...that the family
requested upon arrival.

1489
01:44:02.611 --> 01:44:05.820
The Army has cordoned off
the apartment building where

1490
01:44:05.906 --> 01:44:08.865
they are staying.
The operation has been joined

1491
01:44:08.951 --> 01:44:11.785
by men from the Fiscalía
and the Search Bloc.

1492
01:44:13.622 --> 01:44:15.955
Juan Pablo, please turn it off.

1493
01:44:18.210 --> 01:44:19.997
(Woman)
Do you need anything else?

1494
01:44:21.088 --> 01:44:22.545
No, thank you.

1495
01:44:28.262 --> 01:44:29.173
Pablo!

1496
01:44:37.188 --> 01:44:38.224
Thank you very much.

1497
01:44:38.314 --> 01:44:39.475
You're welcome.

1498
01:45:22.733 --> 01:45:24.645
I should've asked if
anyone wanted anything.

1499
01:45:34.328 --> 01:45:36.570
[phone rings]

1500
01:45:36.664 --> 01:45:37.620
Hello?

1501
01:45:37.706 --> 01:45:38.662
(Agent) Call!

1502
01:45:38.749 --> 01:45:39.956
(Escobar)
Victoria, what happened?

1503
01:45:40.042 --> 01:45:41.203
Are you okay?
Is everyone okay?

1504
01:45:41.293 --> 01:45:43.706
(Victoria) They treated
us well, my love. Don't worry.

1505
01:45:43.796 --> 01:45:45.833
You have to be careful, okay?

1506
01:45:45.923 --> 01:45:48.381
How are they?
How are you? How is Manuela?

1507
01:45:49.343 --> 01:45:50.129
How's Manuela?

1508
01:45:50.219 --> 01:45:52.552
She's okay, my love.
She's okay.

1509
01:45:52.638 --> 01:45:54.675
You're all we
think about, Pablo.

1510
01:45:54.765 --> 01:45:56.973
We miss you so much.

1511
01:45:57.059 --> 01:45:59.096
When you come and go,
are they protecting you?

1512
01:45:59.186 --> 01:46:01.018
Are they holding you hostage?

1513
01:46:01.105 --> 01:46:02.812
(Victoria)
There's an army outside.

1514
01:46:02.898 --> 01:46:03.979
(Agent) Puppy Dog, do you read?

1515
01:46:04.859 --> 01:46:06.225
The man is on the phone.

1516
01:46:06.318 --> 01:46:09.311
La América sector.
I repeat La América sector.

1517
01:46:10.030 --> 01:46:11.271
(Agent) We're on our way, sir.

1518
01:46:13.284 --> 01:46:15.446
Ask the Attorney
General to release you.

1519
01:46:15.536 --> 01:46:16.526
Yes, Attorney General.

1520
01:46:16.620 --> 01:46:19.033
